                <pb facs="0256" n="160" xml:id="pg160"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Conger, through Consul-General at
                        Shanghai.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August 14,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee states that armistice has been asked by Chinese Government, through Li
                    Hung Chang, to which reply has been made that Mr. Conger must first be delivered
                    to relief column at Pekin. The relief column captured Ho-si-wu on August 8, and
                    is supposed now to be near Tung-Chow. Courage.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
